    "method": "core.identityProviderConfigsPartialUpdatePrepare",
    "toolName": "identity-provider-configs-partial-update-prepare",
    "operationId": "identity_provider_configs_partial_update",
    "title": "Update an identity provider configuration (prepare)",
    "category": "Core",
    "description": "Step 1 of 2 for update identity provider configuration. Validates the arguments and returns a signed confirmation_hash plus a message to surface to the user. The user must reply with the literal word \"confirm\" before you call the matching -execute tool with the hash. Original action: Update selected fields on an identity provider configuration by ID. Use this to change SAML, OIDC, SCIM, or XAA (ID-JAG) settings, link selected domains with `organization_domain_ids`, or set `domain_scope: all` to cover all verified organization domains. For selected domains, `organization_domain_ids` replaces the current links. Omit `oidc_client_secret` to keep the saved secret. The update call requires explicit user confirmation.",
